    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined today by **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.67) and **Cal Raleigh** (72.64), who both benefit from ideal platoon alignments and favorable matchups against left-handed arms Jeffrey Springs and Andrew Abbott. **Daulton Varsho** remains a high-floor selection (71.62), as his elite ability to contribute across the board\u2014despite a slight drag from base-running risk against a skilled catcher\u2014keeps him in the \"Strong\" start tier. **Luis Arraez** (64.37) is also locked in, capitalizing on a favorable #1 spot in the order against Michael Wacha, with dynamic platoon factors boosting his expected batting average output.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved leaving **Jonathan Aranda** (52.24) on the bench. While his score was marginally stronger than **Tyler Freeman** (51.83), the optimizer prioritized **Tyler Freeman**'s park factor advantage (+14%) to fill the 2B slot. Elsewhere, we are leaning on the platoon strength of **Taylor Ward** (63.68) and the projected volume for **Bryce Harper** (60.64). Notably, **Ryan Waldschmidt** (59.35) makes the cut despite a suboptimal #9 spot, as the favorable matchup against the lower-tier skill set of Jeffrey Springs outweighs the order penalty. \n\nRisk management remains a priority today, as every position player is currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" We are operating on historical order assumptions; any unexpected shift in the batting order for **Yainer Diaz**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, or **Gavin Sheets** could negatively impact their efficiency scores. **Lawrence Butler** (54.81) carries the highest variance risk today; while the matchup against the weak SP Mitch Bratt provides a high ceiling, the negative platoon split (-13%) against the southpaw necessitates careful monitoring as we balance our game caps.",
